This is the Repository for all data and analysis for the Boredom Project of Project Seminar 1 from Sebastian Kappes
    additional information on the project can be requested via Email under sebastian.kappes@uni-konstanz.de

folder structure was created and connected to git
raw data was downloaded and sorted
three different data origins were identified: LimeSurvey, PsychoPy and Balance files from VR
due to high complexity, all operations leading to the final individual datasets in "master" plus the final complete data set, were conducted in seperated .R scripts, found in the scripts folder
each script has its own workflow .ME file found in the "workflows" folder
    these workflow.ME files give step by step documentation of operation by the code
        also reporting were fixes to data were necessary and when points had to be excluded!
    some of these operations are also explained in each script for better reproducibility
    if necessary, scripts contain checkpoints making sure faults or inconsistencies within the data are spotted.
        through fixing and rerunning, mistakes were found and corrected. -> scripts can be run as they are on raw data and correct all mistakes will be corrected
            if mistakes still occur, warning messages pop up

general workflow
    download raw data
        balance file serves as basis
    run balance.r script
    run psychopy scripts
        psy_file_assumption_checks.r ->for basic file checks and cahnges allowing further work
        psy_pre_management.R -> for file structure and extracting important information, naming standardisation, while creating file copies to keep raw data untouched
        s_file_merging.r -> merging all standardized files into master
    run LimeSurvey scripts
        psy_file_assumption_checks.r ->for cleaning obstructing collums
        limesurvey_processing_with_boredom.r ->for extraction of all necessary LimeSurvey data including demographics, pain, effort, boredom, SBPS, MSBS and attention check
        limesurvey.r -> should ONLY be run if SBPS, MSBS and attention check data is not required
            THIS HAS NOT BEEN RUN IN OUR FINAL DATA SETUP
    run master Script
        master_file_preperation.r -> for creating a single file with all information and data required
            creates a file with 1 line per participant
            creates a file with 2 lines per participant, one for each condition
                in our analysis, condition was deemed more important for sorting results than condition order or measurement block
            -
        -
    run analysis


